A1 L1: with mandrake.rut.patches deployed from the item sha, a load resolves FactionDef RUT_Horrors, IncidentDef RUT_HorrorRaid, GenStepDef RUT_NightHorrorLairs, the four ported forms (ThingDef + PawnKindDef), both bodies, the five lair structures and four crysalises, MapGeneratorDef RUT_HorrorTunnels and GenStepDef RUT_HorrorTunnelNests, and Player.log carries no error line naming RUT_Horror, RUT_NightHorror, RUT_CompHorrorCrysalis or RUT_Horrors.
A2 L2: on a loaded world with nightside land (Ash'karr), a player map freshly generated on a tile whose arc from the substellar point exceeds nightsideBandMinArc + 5 holds at least one RUT_HorrorHive (the lair GenStep ran); its RUT_HorrorSinkhole is the dungeon door into the cave network: going down it (RUT_HorrorSinkholeProbe.Descend, MapPortal.GetOtherMap) opens a RUT_HorrorTunnels pocket map holding at least one hive, crysalis and mite larder and exactly one CaveExit; and RUT_HorrorRaid forced on it fires and leaves pawns of the RUT_Horrors faction on the map.
A3 L2: on the same world, a player map freshly generated on a dayside tile (arc < terminatorBandMinArc - 5) holds no lair structure or crysalis of ours, and RUT_HorrorRaid forced on it reports canFireNow=false (dry run).
